.TH GIT-NEW-BRANCH 1
.SH NAME
git-new-branch \- create a new Git branch using the name provided
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BI "git new-branch " branch-name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a new local branch from the current commit using the specified name.
.PP
The command then handles the remote as follows:
.IP \(bu 2
If a remote is available, it pushes the new branch and configures the local
branch to track it.
.IP \(bu 2
If no remote is available, the branch remains local.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a new branch named
.BR docs/update-readme :
.RS
.nf
git new-branch docs/update-readme
.fi
.RE
